    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (57 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:558`), the create audit line now also logs `membershipNumber` alongside the fields it already recorded:\n\n```java\nAUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}\",\n    owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n    ownerMapper.membershipLevel(owner), ownerMapper.membershipNumber(owner));\n```\n\n`membershipNumber` is derived from the persisted owner via the same `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber(owner)` used for the response DTO, so the logged value matches what the API returns. All previously-logged fields (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`) remain. The new `Cp43Tests` and all 57 existing tests pass.",
